    "title": "John Cena Names The Best Shirt Designs Of His Wrestling Career - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Thomas Lowson ,\n21 minutes ago\nJohn Cena wore dozens of T-shirt designs during his lengthy career with WWE, but some stand out above the rest for the 17-time World Champion.\nAt a recent convention, John was asked to name his five top shirt designs, and joked that it was akin to “asking the Fruity Pebbles to name his favorite cereal.”\nCena first listed a shirt that parodied Super Mario, but said it was because the idea behind the shirt, which was an NFT about Cena, was a total failure.\nREAD MORE: Timeframe For Matt Cardona’s WWE Return, Lexis King Isn’t Happy\nREAD MORE: Val Venis’ Latest Victim Is ….. ?\nJohn then named a shirt that played on the G.I. Joe design, a nostalgic design that the professional wrestling icon called “great.”\nJohn also named his ‘Rise Above Hate’ shirt and his ‘Rise Above Cancer’ shirt, with the latter being named for the amount of money it raised.\nFinally, John named the shirt from his final match in December 2025, highlighting that there are several baseball references hidden in the design.",
    "summary": "John Cena wore dozens of T-shirt designs during his lengthy career with WWE, but some stand out above the rest for the 17-time World Champion. At a recent convention, John was asked to name his five top shirt designs, and joked that it was akin to “asking the Fruity Pebbles to name his favorite cereal.” Cena first listed a shirt that parodied Super Mario, but said it was because the idea behind the shirt, which was an NFT about Cena, was a total failure.",
